{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14262185,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":5,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":5,"pointsAwarded":5,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57975,"firstName":"Harrison","lastName":"Charles","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO3yHD4gcTFRx97dYjQXmX1","sequenceId":19},"course":{"id":111,"name":"Mathematical Foundations II"},"topic":{"id":1110,"name":"The Quotient Rule for Differentiation"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-16T09:45:41.000Z","started":"2026-10-16T09:50:09.000Z","completed":"2026-10-16T09:50:58.000Z","processed":"2026-10-16T09:51:11.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62357801,"created":"2026-10-16T09:50:24.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15564,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:50 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":9909,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":3639,"text":"<p>Given that $y=\\dfrac{1+\\cos x }{\\sin x},$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-\\dfrac{1}{1-\\cos x}$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{1}{1-\\cos x}$","choice3":"$-\\dfrac{1}{1+\\cos x}$","choice4":"$-\\dfrac{1}{\\sin^2 x}$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{1}{\\sin^2 x}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Let $u=1+\\cos x$ and $v=\\sin x.$ Then</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}&=-\\sin x \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad\n\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}=\\cos x.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Using the quotient rule, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\t& = \\dfrac{ v\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}-u\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}}{v^2}\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t& = \\dfrac{(-\\sin x)(\\sin x) - \\cos x(1+\\cos x)}{\\sin^2 x}\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&=\\dfrac{(-\\sin^2 x-\\cos x - \\cos^2 x)}{\\sin^2 x}\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&=\\dfrac{-(\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x)-\\cos x}{\\sin^2 x}.\t\t\t\t\t\n\n}\n\\]\n Since $\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x=1$, we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n\n \\eqalign{\n\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\t\t&=\\dfrac{-1-\\cos x}{\\sin^2 x}\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&=\\dfrac{-(1+\\cos x)}{1-\\cos^2 x}\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&=\\dfrac{- (1+\\cos x)}{(1-\\cos x) (1+\\cos x)}\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{1-\\cos x}.\t\t\t\t\t\n\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":1110,"name":"The Quotient Rule for Differentiation"},"example":{"id":3639,"title":"Differentiating a Quotient Using Leibniz Notation"},"group":{"id":94550,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14262185,"answer":{"id":62357801,"cread":"2026-10-16T09:50:24.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15564},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62357850,"created":"2026-10-16T09:50:40.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12960,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:50 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":11969,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":3639,"text":"<p>Given that $y=\\dfrac{-x}{9-2x}$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-\\dfrac{9}{\\left( 9-2x\\right)^2}$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{9}{\\left( 9-2x\\right)^2}$","choice3":"$-\\dfrac{2x-9}{\\left( 9-2x\\right)^2}$","choice4":"$-\\dfrac{4x-9}{\\left( 9-2x\\right)^2}$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{4x-9}{\\left( 9-2x\\right)^2}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Let $u=-x$ and $v=9-2x.$ Then</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}&=-1 \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad\n\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Using the quotient rule, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\t& = \\dfrac{ v\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}-u\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}}{v^2}\\\\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\left( 9-2x \\right )\\cdot (-1) -(-x)\\cdot (-2)}{\\left( 9-2x\\right)^2}\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{-9+2x-2x}{\\left( 9-2x\\right)^2}\\\\[3pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{9}{\\left( 9-2x\\right)^2}.\n\t\t}\n\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":1110,"name":"The Quotient Rule for Differentiation"},"example":{"id":3639,"title":"Differentiating a Quotient Using Leibniz Notation"},"group":{"id":94546,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14262185,"answer":{"id":62357850,"cread":"2026-10-16T09:50:40.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12960},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62357875,"created":"2026-10-16T09:50:58.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12311,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:50 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":17921,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":3638,"text":"<p> If $f(x) = \\dfrac {\\cos x} {\\ln x},$ find $f'(x).$</p>\n","choice1":"$  \\dfrac {-x\\sin x\\ln x - \\cos x} {x\\ln^2 x} $","choice2":"$  \\dfrac {\\sin x\\ln x - \\cos x} {x\\ln^2 x} $","choice3":"$  \\dfrac {x\\sin x\\ln x - \\cos x} {x\\sin^2 x} $","choice4":"$  \\dfrac {x\\cos x\\ln x - \\cos x} {x\\ln^2 x} $","choice5":"$  \\dfrac {-\\sin x\\ln x - \\sin x} {x\\ln^2 x} $","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x) = \\cos x$ and $v(x) = \\ln x.$ </p>\n<p>Therefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:</p>\n<p>\\begin{eqnarray}\n    \\require{cancel}\n    \\eqalign{\n         f'(x) & = \\dfrac{u'(x)\\cdot v(x) - u(x)\\cdot v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\\\\[3pt]\n \t        & =    \\dfrac {(\\cos x)'\\ln x-(\\cos x)(\\ln x)'} {\\ln^2 x} \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t & 